FROZEN Zero 0.11 native local updater: 126 meaningful checks PASS.
52 native Linux lifecycle/SHA checks; 16 baseline native PE checks under Wine;
9 maximal counter/journal boundary checks; 28 Linux recovery/watch/fault tests;
21 native PE recovery/watch checks under Wine. No arbitrary repetition.

New: flush payloads and journal before successful publication, inspect a valid
complete journal prefix, recover a verified snapshot into a new exclusive
store without changing source, and native foreground local-inbox watch.
Watch detects releases arriving during sleep, uses native wait, stops on error
and holds no update lock while sleeping. No startup scheduler is registered.
Recovery preserves complete selection history/high-water and current/previous
payloads. It reports omitted partial tail bytes and rejects whole bad records.
Source lock, original journal, payloads and unrelated files remain untouched.

Source update.zero SHA256 f06dbaafd26f9bec16250f79c570773d0f327f827eae3980dae46be33a685581
ELF zero-update SHA256 b6c3415f759a01b95d32d2450e6e0d95ad999eb287879e35e1365908a8467a5b
PE zero-update.exe SHA256 d2bb3a320944777e2631e7a5da279c48714288b428ceab1292494a0b5eb2b8af
Compiler SHA256 d89762ea95d3591d95e7f9a66e1015d8124bf87f702dac65ce25547f2ec4ed3f
All four final binaries rebuild byte-for-byte from the final sources.
The exact files above were used for all five final suites. Tests use frozen
0.10 compatible ISO fixtures while root rebuilds 0.11; original user disks are
unchanged. No product code uses Python/shell/CMD/PowerShell at runtime.

Independent source review found no blocker within the documented contract.
A focused partial-write test found an I/O error masked by a later incomplete
hash comparison; fixed by comparing digests only after successful copy I/O.
Linux additionally injects payload/journal fsync failures, native wait failure,
and a concurrent source-journal change. Full records are never dropped during
recovery, including a fully valid latest record whose earlier flush failed.

There is no network fetch/TLS/signature, remote update server, boot activation
or full power-loss guarantee. File fsync/FlushFileBuffers does not synchronize
parent directories or guarantee rename durability. Windows tests use Wine,
not native Windows. See README.txt, FORMAT.txt and summary-0.11.json.
